        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "d6a5eb5f-53f9-5bbe-8fd8-0314f9481df8",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Ozzie Smith, Hank Aaron, Satchel Paige, Omar Vizquel\n- Places: Mobile, Alabama\n- Roles: shortstop\n- Awards: NL Gold Glove Award\n- Topics: baseball records, defensive performance\n\nFacts:\n- Mobile, Alabama popular culture lists Hank Aaron, Ozzie Smith, and Satchel Paige.\n- From 1980 to 1992, Ozzie Smith won the National League Gold Glove Award at shortstop for 13 consecutive seasons.\n- Ozzie Smith was nicknamed \"The Wizard\" for his defensive brilliance.\n- Ozzie Smith set major league records for career assists by a shortstop with 8,375 and double plays by a shortstop with 1,590.\n- Omar Vizquel later broke Ozzie Smith's major league record for double plays by a shortstop.\n- Ozzie Smith set the National League record for 2,511 career games at shortstop.",
